        {
          "type": "kotak",
          "title": "Building a story",
          "items": [
            "Turkish stories are almost always strung together with three words: *önce* (first), *sonra* (then), *en son* (finally). All three go at the start of the sentence.",
            "*Önce Sultanahmet'e gittim. Sonra Ayasofya'yı gördüm. En son vapurla döndüm.* — three short sentences, one complete story. At A1, that's enough to tell the story of your whole day."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
